<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tsarevets</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tsarevets is a fortified hill in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veliko-tarnovo">Veliko Tarnovo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, enclosed by a loop of the Yantra river, which served as the main citadel of the Second Bulgarian Empire from the late 12th century to 1393. Within its walls stood the royal palace and the patriarchal church, as well as houses and monasteries. The fortress was largely destroyed when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took Tarnovo, and its walls and the patriarchal church have since been restored.</p></div>
